  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "hcIngFC0qZqzzp6HUXTyYmz03ZY=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:00.854Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Novabase's qualifying fact is a client: the Portuguese Ministry of Health. That single relationship puts the firm in the right vertical and gives it the right sovereignty exposure, because a national health ministry is exactly the kind of body whose records must stay under its own control and remain auditable after the fact.\n\nEverything else about the firm is unresearched, including its open-source posture and stack, and even its Portuguese headcount is marked unverified. The lead is therefore qualified on exposure and nothing else, which is why it sits at priority 3.\n\nThe reason to keep it is that vertical exposure is the hardest of the qualifying signals to acquire. A firm with the right stack and no sovereignty-exposed clients has to go and win one; a firm with a health-ministry relationship and an unknown stack only has to be screened.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Novabase (PT \u00b7 not verified)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Portuguese Ministry of Health as a client puts it in the right vertical with the right sovereignty exposure. OSS posture unknown.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:00.854820Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:00.854824Z"
    }
  },
